The '''Varkana national football team''' represents [[Varkana]] in international football. It is fielded by the [[Varkana Football Federation]], the governing body of football in Varkana, and competes as a member of MFK, which encompasses the countries of the MOZ. The national team's colours are red, white and green, the colours of the national flag of Varkana, and the borjgali is the symbol of the team.

== History ==

Varkana secured qualification to the World Cup finals due to being co-host of the tournament alongside [[Aetolia]]. They were drawn into a group in which they were considered heavy favourites. On 15 July, Varkana beat Aetolia in the final 4–3 to win the World Cup for the first time. [[Makvala Licheli]] became the first woman to win the World Cup as a coach, while [[David Basilaia]] was awarded the Golden Ball and [[Ari Kenia]] the Golden Boot for their performances during the tournament.

Following the World Cup victory, a few Varkan players announced their retirement from international football, most notably David Basilaia.

== Rivalry ==

Varkana's long-time football rivals are Aetolia. The rivalry is one of the few long-standing football rivalries at a national level and is known as the Sinora derby, named after the Sinora River marking most of the border between the two nations. The rivalry also extends to club level, where Varkan sides have competed frequently against [[É.E. Kavála F.C.]] on the Mesogean level.

== Kit ==

The team kit has been produced by the Breislandic company Adidas since 2004. It is red, white and green to reflect the colours of the Varkan national flag.

== Home stadium ==

[[Erovnul Stadionze]] has been the home ground of the Varkana national football team since its opening on 1 May 1989. Renovated in the late 20th century and early 21st century, most recently in 2018, the stadium has a capacity of 150,000 people, making it the largest stadium in Adonia.

