== Competitive record ==

Varkana's most notable achievement is winning the [[2014 AFA World Cup|2014 World Cup]] on home soil after defeating Aetolia 4–3 in the final. The team also reached the final as co-hosts and have remained one of the best-known sides in the AFA region.

